%N A390006 Integers x such that there exist four integers 0<y<=z<=t<=w such that psi(x)^5 = x^5 + y^5 + z^5 + t^5 + w^5.
%C A390006 The numbers x, y, z, t and w form a psi-quintic quintuple.
%H A390006 Lyle Blosser, <a href="/A390006/a390006_1.txt">File showing RHS values for sequence terms through 31143</a>
%H A390006 S. I. Dimitrov, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.18291">On psi-quadratic k-tuples and their generalizations</a>, arXiv:2509.18291 [math.NT], 2025.
%e A390006 (92, 38, 86, 94, 134) is such a quintuple because psi(92)^5 = 144^5 = 92^5 + 38^5 + 86^5 + 94^5 + 134^5.
